cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use hinode in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: hinode
abstract: >-
  hinode is a Python library for downloading and analyzing observations from
  the Hinode satellite, starting with the X-Ray Telescope (XRT). Observations
  are represented as named-arrays function arrays, so a sequence of images has
  named axes and physical units, and carries the time and sky position of
  every pixel.
authors:
  - family-names: Smart
    given-names: Roy T.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9997-5515"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sun-data/hinode"
url: "https://hinode.readthedocs.io"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - Hinode
  - XRT
  - solar physics
  - data access
